From 7bf097aeebd92b827ff8372208f134981afad5f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:25:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] board: bananapi: add the Banana Pi BPI-M4

The BPI-M4 has an RTD1395, 1 or 2 GiB of DRAM, an SD card slot and
eMMC. The vendor first stage in SPI flash loads U-Boot from the SD
card or the eMMC.

The boot firmware muxes the green status LED pin (ISO GPIO 52) to
another function, and leaves the PMIC bus pins (ISO GPIO 12 and 13)
as GPIOs. Mux them for the LED and for i2c0.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
